Now let me understand the flow. In `getFirstTLVRecord`:
```cpp
TLVRecordType resRec(tlvDataBasePtr); // for NRVO optimization
// resRec pointer is out-bounds of the TLV records memory
if (resRec.getRecordBasePtr() + resRec.getTotalSize() > tlvDataBasePtr + tlvDataLen)
    resRec.assign(NULL);
```

For `PPPoETag`, `getTotalSize()` reads `m_Data->recordLen` (2 bytes at offset 2). If `tlvDataLen` is less than 4 bytes, reading `recordLen` would read beyond the buffer. But the compiler might optimize the two `uint16_t` reads (recordType at offset 0 and recordLen at offset 2) into a single 4-byte read, which would explain the READ 4.

